/* 🔴 F77 · FROZEN 28 Sep 2026 (_handoffs 7042c77, RR-81) and AMENDED (Amendment 1, _handoffs b443e5e, owner ruling RR-82 §2 a726cc3):
 * R2 replaced — a retry of the SAME operation identity never reissues a metered query or repeats a save; a FRESH authorised collection
 * is a new operation. Paid call paths are OUT of the current scope: NOT MEASURED (config/fboard/deferred-limbs.mjs holds the checkable
 * reopening trigger). The original stays pinned as F77_ORIGINAL and is named by both hashes. Pinned from the committed blobs by
 * parseContract (derivation re-run with a firing control inside each contract). */
export const F77_ORIGINAL = Object.freeze({
  featureId: "F77",
  ruling: Object.freeze({ repo: "_handoffs", path: "AlmiVisibility_F77_ACCEPTANCE_2026-09-28.md", commit: "7042c77f812777a1866ed52ad81ede5d3fcd2438", sha256: "35f921a91dfee8e6dc46764e3a5c3cb51aa7b70d565736a951a155dea87df4ef" }),
  authority: Object.freeze({ propositionId: "F77_ACCEPTANCE", scope: Object.freeze(["ALMIVISIBILITY", "F77"]) }),
  frozenOn: "2026-09-28",
  feature: "F77 · Idempotency retry and rollback safety",
  input: "Every durable writer in the engine's real tree — every code path that appends, creates, replaces or removes a durable record, file, store entry, trail event or cost entry — and every code path able to issue a paid or metered call; each driven with the same logical request twice in sequence, twice concurrently, and again after a crash at every declared step boundary and after recovery.",
  expected: "[R1 · ONE RECORD] For every durable writer, repeating the same logical write — in sequence or concurrently, or re-running it after a crash and recovery — leaves exactly ONE logical record and ONE of each side-effect event it owes; a repeat returns the already-committed outcome instead of writing again.\n[R2 · ONE PAID CALL] A paid or metered call is issued at most once per logical request identity across every retry and recovery; a repeat after an issued call never re-issues it; and none is issued at all without the owner's approval.\n[R3 · NOTHING DESTROYED] No retry and no recovery deletes, truncates, overwrites or reorders a committed record, a trail event or its evidence; an append-only store is only ever appended to.\n[R4 · RECOVERY IS SAFE AND REPEATABLE] After a crash at any step boundary, recovery reaches exactly one consistent state — the write committed exactly once, or exposed as an incomplete attempt — never a half-written record silently kept or silently discarded; running recovery again changes nothing further.\n[R5 · CENSUS] Every durable writer and every paid-capable call path in the real tree is enumerated, each with the mechanism that makes it safe under R1–R4 or the refusal that prevents it acting; the population and the bound are printed beside the result, and an unclassified writer or call path fails the census.\n[R6 · RECORDED] Every outcome of a repeat or a recovery — committed, already committed, refused, incomplete attempt exposed, recovered — is recorded through the audit trail exactly once.",
  failure: "[R1] A repeat, a concurrent repeat, or a re-run after recovery leaves a second logical record or a second side-effect event, or writes again instead of returning the committed outcome. [R2] A paid or metered call is issued twice for one logical request, re-issued after a retry or a recovery, or issued without the owner's approval. [R3] A retry or a recovery deletes, truncates, overwrites or reorders a committed record, trail event or evidence, or rewrites an append-only store. [R4] A crash leaves a half-written record kept or discarded silently, recovery reaches more than one state, or a second recovery changes anything. [R5] A durable writer or paid-capable call path is missing from the census, unclassified, or classified without a mechanism; or the census prints a figure without its population and bound. [R6] An outcome goes unrecorded, or is recorded twice. And for any limb: it is proved only on an empty population, or only by a control that cannot fire; or a test that fails under parallel load is set aside without evidence for why.",
  evidence: "For each limb: a test driving the production path; a firing control; and a sabotage that removes the limb in the bytes, turns a named test red for that reason, and is restored by raw-byte hash with the production trail untouched. Concurrency proved with genuinely parallel processes against confined stores, never the production trail. Crash recovery proved by an injected failure at each declared step boundary. The census run over the real tree, count-only, with its bound and a firing control. The paid-call limb proved on every real paid-capable call path with a non-networked stand-in provider, never a real paid, metered or live call; if that population is EMPTY, the limb is COULD-NOT-PROVE, never PASS. The repeat-write failure seen under parallel load explained by evidence, and repaired if it is a defect in this territory. The full suite as CI runs it, and exact-SHA CI on the PR head before any merge, then on the merge commit. F77 moves only through the production validator and the audit trail, and only when every limb is PROVED.",
  contractSha256: "e315b39e0cf24a0de4444a6c0be6636d249e56843eed56018c157b99c9992115",
});

