    input: "Every registered sealed held-out role: each HELD_OUT_EVIDENCE entry, each MARKING_KEY entry, and each\nRETIRED_CONTAMINATED population, each with its registered identity, derivation or sealed path, content hash,\naccess rule and population accounting; the existing declared held-out evaluation set and protocol inputs,\nunchanged; a mechanism that must be assessed without its builders or mandatory governance readers seeing the\nheld-out payload or its labels. In addition: each MARKING_KEY's explicit link to exactly one registered\nHELD_OUT_EVIDENCE set, and the tenant scope of both; the location of every sealed payload, whether a git-tracked\nsealed path or another governed sealed store; a frozen scorer identified by id and hash; and a scoring request\nnaming the set, its linked marking key, both commitments, the scope, the authorised evaluator, the frozen\nmechanism and the frozen scorer.\nIn addition (Amendment 3): a PAIRED protocol, declared by the frozen scorer, in which every item of the registered set is a pair of an initial need and a candidate, and a re-paired item also names the matched pair it was drawn from; and, for every item, the frozen mechanism's explicit answer — a class list, or an explicit ABSTAIN.",
    expected: "Every existing F07 behaviour holds unchanged: refusal before filesystem read of every sealed path, recorded\naccess, freeze before access, complete scoring accounting, post-access contamination refusal, and the retired-\npopulation census. In addition, the governance and content leak census enumerates EVERY registered sealed\nHELD_OUT_EVIDENCE and MARKING_KEY entry, not only retired populations, and scans governance text, commands,\ntests, fixtures, logs and reports for any member of a held-out set and for any label or marking-key content.\nThe marking-key store is a role distinct from the held-out set; the implementer's role never reads it; the\ndetector for it runs inside the sealed boundary and reports only that a leak exists, its category and its\nlocation, never what leaked. LINKED GRANT: a scoring grant covers exactly one registered HELD_OUT_EVIDENCE set\ntogether with its explicitly linked, distinct MARKING_KEY; the two identities, their commitments, the tenant\nscope and the authorised evaluator are bound in one recorded grant before any access. GOVERNED READ: every read\nof either side goes through the sealed lifecycle and records a durable ACCESS event before the value is used;\nitem-level comparison happens only inside the boundary; no payload and no item-level result crosses out of it,\nan item-level result being any value tied to an individual item: its identity, position, label, output or\ncomparison outcome. AGGREGATE SCORE: the only released result is what the frozen scorer emits: count-only\nper-class TP, FP, FN and TN tables, the denominator, the exclusion counts, the evidence state, the mechanism,\nscorer and software versions, and the audit provenance; a count cell that is zero or equal to the denominator\nstates a fact true of every item, and is released as the aggregate it is; exactly one valid scoring run exists\nper frozen combination of set, mechanism, scorer and marking-key commitment, claimed on the trail before any\ncomparison. COMPLETE CENSUS: the registry and the leak census cover both roles, whether the sealed payload is\ngit-tracked or held in another governed sealed store; registration yields a discoverable manifest of\nidentities, links, locations, counts and commitments without exposing any value; a direct read inside a\ngoverned path cannot bypass recorded access. THE LIMIT, STATED PLAINLY: activity outside the governed paths,\nincluding an independent git show or a direct file read by any person or tool, cannot be observed by F07 and is\nnot claimed to be.\nPAIRED RELEASE (Amendment 3): for a paired protocol only, the linked evaluator, inside the sealed boundary, may derive and release exactly THREE additional count-only aggregates — abstentions, discordant pairs, and discordant pairs correct in both directions — and nothing else; they are bound to the same registered set and key, the same denominator, the same scorer version, the same once-only run and the same durable ACCESS trail as the per-class tables, and a count that is zero or equal to its population is released as the aggregate it is. An explicit ABSTAIN is a distinct, validated answer: it stays in the denominator, is scored as not-positive in every per-class table, is counted as an abstention, and is never counted as a negative answer. The pair structure is parsed only inside the boundary and never released; no item identity, pair, label, prediction, set membership or reconstructable item-level value crosses out. PREFLIGHT: every set-side and key-side input — registered, readable, the set commitment, the key commitment, parseable, consistent and COMPLETE for every set item — is checked BEFORE the run is claimed, and a fault refuses the request without consuming the once-only run; a missing or invalid mechanism output still invalidates the claimed run. The metadata ceiling holds: a paired protocol carries at most seven class and exclusion tokens. Every other clause holds unchanged except where this release extension expressly applies.",
